## `ns` Form

### Canonical `ns` form shape

```clojure
(ns examples.ns
  (:refer-clojure :exclude [next replace remove])
  (:require [clojure.string :as s :refer [blank?]]
            [clojure.set :as set]
            [clojure.java.shell :as sh])
  (:import java.util.Date
           java.text.SimpleDateFormat
           [java.util.concurrent Executors
                                 LinkedBlockingQueue]))
```

### `:require` preference order

Prefer in this order:

1. `:require :as`                   ← default choice
2. `:require :refer [specific syms]`  ← when a few names need to be bare
3. `:require :refer :all`             ← rare, only when warranted
4. `:use`                             ← **deprecated**, do not use in new code

✅ Good — `:as`:

```clojure
(ns examples.ns
  (:require [clojure.zip :as zip]))
```

✅ Good — `:refer` with specific symbols:

```clojure
(ns examples.ns
  (:require [clojure.zip :refer [lefts rights]]))
```

⚠️ Acceptable only as warranted — `:refer :all`:

```clojure
(ns examples.ns
  (:require [clojure.zip :refer :all]))
```

❌ Bad — `:use` is deprecated:

```clojure
(ns examples.ns
  (:use clojure.zip))
```

